#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0709 expect=noViolation domain=ADSL
#note "CR709 (ADaM Conformance Rules v5.0, ADaMIG 1.2/1.3): a column spelled TRTXXP - the template itself, upper-cased - resolves case-insensitively to the Library's TRTxxP as a LITERAL hit: it names no concrete variable, there are no digits to substitute, and the library serves no label template for it (label_template(\"LIBRARY\") is empty), so the rule's not empty(label_template(\"LIBRARY\")) guard keeps it out whatever its label -> silent (PLAN-library-template-label-resolution). A real period instance, TRT01P, IS checked (-invalid_lowercase_indexed_name). STUDYID is the positive control."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADSL STUDYID name=STUDYID label="Study Identifier"
#library variable-metadata ADSL TRTxxP name=TRTxxP label="Planned Treatment for Period xx"
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col TRTXXP  type=Char label="Wrong Label"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | Placebo
---
